            "block_reason": "CD-48 authorises these two trust-surface repairs (owner ruling 2026-09-15: prohibition is fine but allow leeway). The block itself is correct and is NOT disputed: a run may never modify the verifier trust surface, so this change is the Chair's, made under the owner's ruling. Provenance note, stated rather than hidden: the flash run was killed when its terminal was cleaned up, so its exit code was never observed; I passed --exit=1 to close the record and the ledger classified the run blocked on scope regardless. The partial work it left was independently verified before adoption - both repairs behave, tests/ai_autonomy_test.php 78/78, ai_run_test 79/79, ai_project_test 18/18, and the new --existed-at-dispatch flag refuses malformed values.",
