            "run_id": "admin-chrome",
            "block_reason": "Two offences are mine (CE-12): the contract listed the shell manifest but not the seo/navigation manifests, and a capability consumer MUST declare the dependency in its own module.json, so those edits were unavoidable. Legitimised by contract revision 3 under CD-57, not by silently widening the envelope. The third offence on cms-akira-shell/module.json is the known D-2 defect where finish() cannot receive a justification. Verified live by the chair: seo 2094->6647 and navigation 3102->7531, both now carry the sidebar, exactly one Tailwind load, every form field preserved, shell users page byte-identical at 9993.",
