        {
            "run_id": "admin-shell-integrity",
            "block_reason": "The cms-akira-theme/module.json edit is the dependency declaration a capability consumer must make and is listed in this contract's Files likely affected; the L4 classification is the known D-2 defect where finish() cannot receive a justification. Chair-verified live WITH a cache-buster: aside no longer absolute, nav scrolls (955 in 385), Sign out at y=506 below the nav box 100-485, VISUAL collisions empty. My first two probes produced a false defect - one measured cached HTML, the other compared raw geometry and ignored overflow-y-auto clipping. The new spec falsified pre-fix at 900px (Site settings, Provenance) and 600px (Permissions). Theme Studio remains sidebarless pending the caller-widening route, which is an owner decision recorded in CD-58.",
            "director_decision": "CD-58",
